<title>UK: CRICKET-SUNDAY LEAGUE RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SUNDAY LEAGUE RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the latest round of</p>
<p>Sunday League cricket matches:</p>
<p>At Hove: Essex beat Sussex by 8 wickets. Sussex 216-6</p>
<p>innings complete - 40 overs (R.Rao 60, K.Greenfield 58 not out).</p>
<p>Essex 220-2 in 30.2 overs (S.Law 123, P.Prichard 68).</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Warwickshire beat Derbyshire by 108 runs.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 201-6 innings complete - 21 overs (N.Smith 60,</p>
<p>D.Brown 57). Derbyshire 93 all out in 16.5 overs.</p>
<p>At Glamorgan: Glamorgan beat Middlesex by 6 wickets.</p>
<p>Middlesex 185-6 innings closed - 40 overs. Glamorgan 186-4 in</p>
<p>35.3 overs (M.Maynard 71 not out).</p>
<p>At The Oval: Surrey beat Yorkshire by 5 wickets. Yorkshire</p>
<p>198-9 innings complete - 40 overs (D.Lehmann 56). Surrey 199-5</p>
<p>in 38.3 overs (G.Thorpe 100 not out).</p>
<p>At Basingstoke: Somerset beat Hampshire by 6 runs. Somerset</p>
<p>175 all out in 40 overs. Hampshire 169-9 in 40 overs (J.Kerr</p>
<p>4-28).</p>
<p>At Bristol: Gloucestershire beat Worcestershire by 1 run.</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 177 all out in 38.3 overs (R.Cuncliffe 50;</p>
<p>S.Lampitt 4-49). Worcestershire 176-7 in 40 overs (D.Leatherdale</p>
<p>51).</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire beat Kent by 17 runs. Lancashire</p>
<p>172-3 innings complete - 35 overs (M.Atherton 90 not out). Kent</p>
<p>155 all out in 34 overs (T.Ward 53).</p>
